One file in each variant directory is a vendored copy:

  extra-manifests/local-path-provisioner.yaml.tpl
      Generated from k3s' packaged local-storage manifest by
      scripts/vendor-local-path.sh, which records the source URL and every
      transformation in the file's own header. The manifest deploys
      rancher/local-path-provisioner; both projects are Apache-2.0.

Neither upstream repository publishes a NOTICE file (checked at the pinned k3s tag and at
local-path-provisioner's default branch: both return 404), so there are no upstream
attribution notices to propagate beyond the attribution above.

This copy exists because k3s re-applies its own packaged manifest on every start, which
resets the default-StorageClass annotation. The reasoning is in the generated file's
header and in docs/RUNBOOK.md; the cost is that this repository, not k3s, is now
responsible for keeping the manifest current.

